@startuml
!include ../style.iuml
autonumber
title Sequence 1 — Donor sign-up with phone OTP

actor Donor
participant "Web / mobile app" as App
participant "POST /api/auth/otp/*\nPOST /api/auth/signup" as Api
participant "OtpService" as Otp
database "Redis" as Redis
participant "SMS gateway" as Sms
participant "SignUpDonorHandler" as H
database "SQL Server" as Sql

Donor -> App : phone number
App -> Api : otp/request (purpose = Signup)
Api -> Otp : request code (rate limited per client and per phone)
Otp -> Redis : TTL of outstanding code (60 s resend cooldown)
Otp -> Redis : HMSET otp:{purpose}:{phone}\nh = SHA-256(code), att = 0, EXPIRE 5 min
note right of Redis : only the hash is stored;\nthe code never touches SQL
Otp -> Sql : SMS template for purpose + language
Otp -> Sql : notify.Notifications row (DedupKey) before sending
Otp -> Sms : "Your Sethika code is …"
Sms --> Donor : SMS

Donor -> App : 6-digit code
App -> Api : otp/verify
Api -> Otp : verify
Otp -> Redis : compare hash, count attempt
alt wrong code
  Otp --> App : 400 (after 5 wrong attempts: otp_attempts_exhausted)
else right code
  Otp -> Redis : delete code, store otp:ticket:{purpose}:{phone}\n= SHA-256(ticket), 15 min
  Otp --> App : 200 { ticket }
end

Donor -> App : name, password, consent to legal documents
App -> Api : signup { ticket, ... }
Api -> H : SignUpAsync
H -> H : validate phone, name, email, language,\npassword policy, consent (no ticket spent yet)
H -> Otp : RedeemTicketAsync
Otp -> Redis : Lua script: delete ticket only if hash matches (atomic)
alt ticket invalid / already used
  H --> App : 400
end
H -> Sql : phone already registered?
alt yes
  H --> App : 409 already_registered\n(said only to someone who proved they hold the phone)
end
H -> Sql : one SaveChanges (one transaction):\nauth.Users (PhoneConfirmed), DonorProfiles,\nUserRoles (DONOR), UserConsents,\nOutboxMessage DonorSignedUp
H --> Api : user
Api -> Api : issue JWT + refresh token (new family)
Api --> App : 201, refresh token in httpOnly cookie\n(mobile: in the body, kept in secure store)
@enduml
